  "license": "LGPL-3.0",
  "comments": "Bi-level (PC-AC) mechanical ventilation on a single-compartment lung. Airway pressure alternates between Pinsp and PEEP; the lung (resistance R, compliance C) responds as a first-order system, giving the decelerating inspiratory flow and the tidal volume of pressure-controlled ventilation. A periodic patient effort (Pmus) is added at each inspiration onset to emulate an assisted breath. Scopes show Pressure / Flow / Volume like a ventilator screen; the XY scope draws the dynamic pressure-volume loop. Settings: PEEP 5, Pinsp 18 cmH2O, RR 15/min, Ti 1.2 s (Width 30%), R 10 cmH2O.s/L, C 0.05 L/cmH2O (tau = R*C = 0.5 s) -> Vt ~ 0.6 L.",
  "name": "Medical Ventilator - Bi-level (PC-AC) with simulated patient",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "pv",
      "type": "pulse",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 160,
      "rotation": 0,
      "params": { "Amplitude": 13, "Period": 4, "Width": 30, "StartTime": 0, "Offset": 0 }
    },
